mongoc-error-reply-one-pass - a reply's error fields found in one pass

_parse_error_reply() looked for "code", "errmsg", "$err" and "writeConcernError" with four bson_iter_init_find
calls - four walks over the reply, for every reply, and a successful reply has none of them, so each walk went to
its end. One walk records the first occurrence of each now (as bson_iter_find does) and the rest of the function
reads those. Which field wins, the types accepted, the write concern error's own lookups: unchanged.

Measured (coraine, mongo 8.2.12, user-space instructions per request, perf stat): PATCH -7,669, retrieve -3,180 (after 0001-0002).

